# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS & CREDENTIALS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env files may contain DATABASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# ADMIN_API_KEY, SESSION_SECRET — all of which grant
# direct access to the production database and LLM billing.
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.production
.env.development
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RUNTIME DATA & STATE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pilot database (SQLite) stores session transcripts,
# audit logs, and potentially PII-adjacent data.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# Directory exclusions below use the `yourpeer-chatbot/<name>` prefix
# because the build command packages the directory from its parent:
#   tar czf out.tar.gz --exclude-from=yourpeer-chatbot/.tarignore yourpeer-chatbot/
# Under this invocation, an unanchored pattern like `data/` silently
# does nothing on GNU tar and matches by basename on BSD tar
# (macOS default) — which on BSD tar would silently exclude
# backend/app/rag/data/ (the NYC boroughs GeoJSON loaded at runtime
# by boundaries.py). The prefixed form is the only portable way to
# mean "only the top-level data/ directory."
#
# This bit us once — see docs/CLAUDE.md about app.models being
# silently `.tarignore`'d in a prior release.
#
# If the directory is ever renamed, update these prefixes.
yourpeer-chatbot/pilot_data
yourpeer-chatbot/data
 
# Session transcripts — may contain redacted but
# still sensitive conversation content.
#
# Be careful with these patterns: a bare `*transcript*` matched
# `transcript-drawer.tsx` (a frontend admin component) and silently
# dropped it from the tarball, breaking the production build because
# `conversation-table.tsx` imports it. The patterns below are
# anchored to data-file extensions so source files with "transcript"
# in the name aren't caught.
transcripts/
*transcript*.json
*transcript*.jsonl
*transcript*.csv
*transcript*.txt
*transcript*.log
*session_data*
*conversation_log*
 
# Eval result files — contain scenario transcripts
# that may reference real service locations.
eval_results/
*eval_run*
# The loose eval_report.json at the repo root (written by the
# admin panel's "Run Evals" button) also contains full scenario
# transcripts and should never ship in a tarball.
eval_report.json
eval_report*.json
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KEYS & CERTIFICATES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cert
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PYTHON ARTIFACTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.cover
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MACOS ARTIFACTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
._*
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EDITOR & IDE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.settings/
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VERSION CONTROL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPENDENCIES (reinstallable)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# node_modules/ is left unprefixed on purpose — npm legitimately
# nests it (e.g., backend/node_modules/, frontend-next/node_modules/)
# and we want them all excluded. A trailing-slash unanchored pattern
# matches by basename under BSD tar, which is the behavior we want
# here.
#
# venv directories use the `yourpeer-chatbot/` prefix (see RUNTIME
# DATA section for rationale). Listed at the two conventional
# locations used by this project.
node_modules/
.npm/
yourpeer-chatbot/venv
yourpeer-chatbot/.venv
yourpeer-chatbot/env
yourpeer-chatbot/backend/venv
yourpeer-chatbot/backend/.venv
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOGS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MODEL ARTIFACTS (large, downloadable)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Semantic router model (~80MB) is downloaded at
# startup from HuggingFace. Don't ship it.
*.onnx
*.bin
*.pt
*.safetensors
# Prefixed form — see RUNTIME DATA section above for why.
# Without the `yourpeer-chatbot/` prefix, BSD tar treats `models/` as
# "match any directory named models" and silently excludes
# backend/app/models/ — which is the Pydantic schema package the app
# imports at startup, NOT a model artifacts directory.
yourpeer-chatbot/sentence-transformers
yourpeer-chatbot/models
 
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MUTATION TESTING ARTIFACTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# cosmic-ray stores session state in SQLite files. `make mutation`
# creates one per module (cr-backend-app-services-classifier.sqlite
# etc.). These can be 100KB+ each and contain copies of the mutated
# source along with per-mutant test output — useful locally, no value
# in a shipped tarball.
cr.sqlite
cr-*.sqlite
 
# cosmic-ray.toml is generated fresh by `make mutation-module` from
# the per-module template in the Makefile, so there's nothing to ship
# — the Makefile is the source of truth.
cosmic-ray.toml
 
# mutmut v3 copies the source tree into mutants/ when a run starts
# and stashes a SQLite stats cache in .mutmut-cache. We use cosmic-ray
# now, but someone running mutmut against this codebase would create
# both. Neither should ship.
mutants/
.mutmut-cache
.mutmut-cache/